mary jane baleazza explains how the  center in the southeast valley helping  child care providers and their families  at the height of covid 19 many child  care businesses closed impacting access  to affordable and quality care for many  families child care provider gail  thompson says the grand opening of  nevada's strong start couldn't have come  in a better time there's licensing help  there's urban league for parents there's  if we have any questions or we need help  doing something  they're here for us nevada's strong  start child care services center is a  one-stop hub providing support and  resources it's something providers say  is much needed during this pandemic  during the pandemic there was a lot of  shutdown so we didn't know like legally  what we needed to do a natural law is  also a child care provider she turned to  nevada strong start to use its resources  to establish an in-home child care  center no one has to spend countless  hours  calling around trying to find where do  you do these things and it just it would  help cut down on the confusion that  takes place because sometimes you can  get information  and it might not be vital thompson says  she knows the struggle families face she  supplies 24 hour child services and is  providing relief for her own family by  watching her granddaughter a lot of my  parents are essential workers anywhere  from front line you know working in  hospitals so i'm just really happy that  we do have better resources now they've  always been there but it's just been  hard to find those resources reporting  from spencer and flamingo mary jane  balleza live local now  nevada strong start is the first of its  kind to open up in las vegas a second  location is slated to open up in reno  this year
 

